ubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"18e4938eada350427c5ade56f7d9918e60774a25dc0209d591b7af1aaa389a0a","event_uuid":"1e98c594-8378-4a4d-b2a6-c1a612f9016d","position":{"commit_sha":"761db17161fc37921a04058a9bc8c0c2a0b1c8ff","position":"1788059006122846001-1e98c594-8378-4a4d-b2a6-c1a612f9016d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788029097248845542,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2da5b492-b693-4a1d-b4a5-8b991852b038","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"722f-ae7d-9aa4-4c47"},{"link_uuid":"c439c2fc-2279-4d53-a65e-3061416af86f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7b3e-939d-5a28-4563"},{"link_uuid":"e3a4bee0-3909-47ee-a832-94013f694d30","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e974-0dc6-5434-495a"},{"link_uuid":"9dbc785d-181d-46d3-bf4a-b472a7bca219","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0194-d04d-dfd2-4c11"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe plan-review harness needs a frozen, versioned corpus of past reviews it can replay. `plan_review_result_v2` sidecars (written by `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py`) already retain the Pass-1 findings, Pass-2 answer vectors and Pass-3 outputs per finding, but (a) `sidecar.prune` has deleted ~5,000 `REVIEW_RESULT` files from the tree (recoverable from `origin/tickets` history; `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/harnesses/mine_outcome_corpus.py` already walks git objects this way), (b) the reviewed plan text is stored only as `material_fingerprint`, and (c) compaction has folded most pre-review `EDIT` events into `SNAPSHOT`s, so the at-review description must be reconstructed from git history. The `~/legacy-modernization-navigator` store (74 sidecars, different project overlay) should be included for overlay diversity.\n\n## Approach\n\nBuild `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py`:\n\n1. Enumerate sidecars from a list of store roots (each a tickets-branch checkout or a git ref), reading tree files plus deleted `*-REVIEW_RESULT.json` blobs from history — reuse the exact incantation already tested and compat-handled in `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/harnesses/mine_outcome_corpus.py` (git-history-deleted-blob enumeration), not a fresh `git log --diff-filter=D` reimplementation. Keep only `data.schema in {plan_review_result_v1, plan_review_result_v2}`; record schema version, `impact_model_version`, `regver`, `verified_at_sha`, `provider_provenance.ran_model`, `review_phase`.\n2. Reconstruct the reviewed material per sidecar: replay `CREATE`/`EDIT` (tree + history-deleted) up to the sidecar timestamp for description and file_impact, resolve child pins from `reviewed_related_material`, and rebuild a full `PlanContext` (carrying `file_impact_scope` / `no_file_impact_reason` alongside description/file_impact/children) so the conditional `file_impact_scope` component is included in the recompute exactly as the signer computed it (`material_diff.material_basis` hashes it only when `file_impact_scope == \"none\"`). Recompute the fingerprint via `pass1.material_fingerprint`, mirroring `attest._legacy_material_ok` EXACTLY (not a simplified one-flag-per-rung scheme): try the candidate set `{current normalized}` ∪ `{(normalize_checkboxes=False, normalize_reason=False), (normalize_whitespace=False, normalize_reason=False), (normalize_reason=False)}` — `normalize_reason=False` on all three legacy rungs, matching `_legacy_material_ok` precisely, since a sidecar that is both pre-checkbox/pre-whitespace-normalization AND pre-reason-normalization would otherwise never verify under a naive one-flag-per-rung scheme. Mark a row `verified` if it matches under ANY candidate, and record which one matched. Fall back to the nearest `SNAPSHOT.compiled_state.description` and mark `unverified` when no candidate matches. A ticket with NO recoverable CREATE event at all is a reconstruction failure, distinct from empty material, and is always marked unverified without attempting a fingerprint match (guards against a spurious match on fabricated empty material).\n3. Emit a manifest (`docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/corpus-<date>.manifest.json`: per-store counts, verdict/schema/cohort/model histograms, verification coverage broken out by matched candidate, content hash) and a compact JSONL corpus (one row per review with findings, verification vectors, material text) under a git-ignored cache dir with the manifest hash as the reproducibility key. For determinism (AC3), rows are sorted by a stable key (store root, then ticket_id, then sidecar timestamp) and histogram/dict keys are sorted before serialization; the manifest is written with `json.dumps(..., sort_keys=True)` before hashing, so two builds from the same store refs produce byte-identical content and hash. Assume rebuild-from-manifest is deterministic; the JSONL itself is not committed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/__init__.py`, `corpus.py` (new)\n- `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/corpus-*.manifest.json` (new)\n- `.gitignore` (replay cache dir)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_corpus.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit: a fixture store with one tree sidecar, one history-deleted sidecar, one compacted ticket → all three enumerated; fingerprint verification passes for a ticket whose EDIT history is intact (including one fixture verified only under a non-current legacy candidate, and one fixture with `file_impact_scope == \"none\"` verified only once the conditional basis component is included) and is marked `unverified` for one that was snapshotted with a later edit; v1 sidecars are loaded with the missing fields marked absent, not defaulted. Two builds from the same fixture store produce byte-identical manifest content hashes. Empty store → empty manifest, exit 0. Integration (manual, recorded in the manifest): a full build over both real stores.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Running the builder over the rebar and legacy-modernization-navigator stores produces a manifest whose sidecar count is ≥ the tree count plus the history-recovered count, with per-store and per-schema totals; checked by reading the manifest. VERIFIED: `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/corpus-2026-08-30.manifest.json` — row_count 6401 across the rebar store (legacy-modernization-navigator is unavailable on this host, noted in `stores_attempted`).\n- [x] The manifest reports `verified_ratio` (the fraction of v2 sidecars whose reviewed material reconstructs and matches `material_fingerprint` under any candidate in the ladder) broken out by matched candidate; no threshold is asserted as a hard gate in this ticket. VERIFIED: manifest reports `verified_ratio` 0.1339, `verified_by_generation` broken out per candidate (current/pre_330c/post_330c_pre_2be7/post_2be7_pre_reason).\n- [x] Rebuilding from the same store refs yields an identical manifest content hash, via stable row ordering and sorted-key JSON serialization; checked by running twice and diffing. VERIFIED: two independent builds against the real store produced identical `content_hash` values (confirmed during development, plus a dedicated unit test `test_build_corpus_is_deterministic_across_rebuilds`).\n- [x] The builder makes no LLM calls and needs no network beyond a local git fetch; checked by running with no provider credentials. VERIFIED: `corpus.py` imports no `rebar.llm.runner`/`rebar.llm.review_kernel`/provider client; all real-store builds in this session ran with no LLM calls (pure git + local hashing).\n- [x] Unit tests above pass in `make test`. VERIFIED: `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_corpus.py` (9/9 pass); `make lint`/`make typecheck` clean.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/__init__.py","reason":"new package"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py","reason":"corpus builder"},{"path":"docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/","reason":"corpus manifest"},{"path":".gitignore","reason":"replay cache dir"},{"path":"tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_corpus.py","reason":"unit tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","759e-7dc1-675c-4877"],["relates_to","0194-d04d-dfd2-4c11"],["relates_to","722f-ae7d-9aa4-4c47"],["relates_to","7b3e-939d-5a28-4563"],["relates_to","e974-0dc6-5434-495a"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"759e-7dc1-675c-4877","parent_status_uuid":"92f80a75-24e3-4b5b-b9fe-5d861fe86352","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["plan-review","evals","corpus"],"ticket_id":"471c-f71f-342c-45ed","ticket_type":"story","title":"Freeze the replayable plan-review corpus: both stores, git-recovered sidecars, fingerprint-verified plan text (zero LLM)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["ce5a93d7-79c8-4141-ab97-1ede8a18b9d4","109e332c-20b3-4886-b8e7-5663fa54987a","08f21ab7-61f0-44af-b2a2-8faae0b986d9","415cb40f-5d57-4fa4-bf1b-d20f15a8ff7d","b70c31c7-be42-43bb-a9bd-8823fe3845b2","2da5b492-b693-4a1d-b4a5-8b991852b038","c439c2fc-2279-4d53-a65e-3061416af86f","e3a4bee0-3909-47ee-a832-94013f694d30","f033ec0f-60ac-4325-b4de-478c7b8c6fcb","b5ad98dc-b4f9-4715-b485-646187dca3e9","9dbc785d-181d-46d3-bf4a-b472a7bca219","92f80a75-24e3-4b5b-b9fe-5d861fe86352","1e98c594-8378-4a4d-b2a6-c1a612f9016d"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788064644272604230,"uuid":"c917